  "headline": "Indonesia Formally Enacts Law On Asset Seizure For Criminal Cases",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Enacts Law On Asset Seizure",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has passed the Asset Seizure Law, which grants authorities power to confiscate assets linked to criminal activities.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Indonesian House of Representatives officially passed the Asset Seizure Law during a plenary session led by the Speaker of the House.",
    "The new legislation allows for the confiscation of assets related to various crimes, including corruption, terrorism, and online gambling.",
    "Parliamentary leaders confirmed the exclusion of illicit enrichment provisions, drawing criticism from transparency advocacy groups."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has officially passed the Asset Seizure Law, a major legislative development aimed at addressing various criminal activities. According to parliamentary leaders, the law grants authorities the power to confiscate assets connected to crimes such as corruption, terrorism, and online gambling, with or without a prior court verdict. While the legislation marks a significant expansion of state seizure powers, it has also sparked debate regarding its specific provisions. Notably, the final version excludes regulations concerning illicit enrichment by public officials, a move that has drawn public criticism from anti-corruption organizations like Indonesia Corruption Watch. Regional legal institutions, such as the West Nusa Tenggara High Prosecutor's Office, have indicated they are already reviewing the newly established statutory requirements to determine how they will be applied to pending criminal cases moving forward.",
